<title>UK: UK's ITC awards BSkyB unit Channel 5 text.</title>
<headline>UK's ITC awards BSkyB unit Channel 5 text.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>British broadcasting regulator, the Independent Television Commission, said on Friday it had awarded the single licence to provide the additional text service on Channel 5 to Sky Five Text Ltd, a joint venture between British Sky Broadcasting and Channel 5.  </p>
<p>The licence is for 10 years and was bid for 1.5 million stg.</p>
<p>ITC said it expected the service will commence no later than June 30, 1998.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
</text>
